    Commit and sample the folded parameter row before drawing its columns
    
    Each parameter table claim now folds the single table row, commits the folded
    message as G_u with its own code, pads, tails, salts and runtime tree, absorbs
    the root, draws and absorbs the sample answers, and only then draws the table
    columns and opens them. The verifier replays the same order, compares the
    seeds and positions and verifies the openings against the plan reader. The
    claims are single-row only in this stage; a packed multi-row table is rejected
    at plan validation. The fixture attaches a legal fold shape to both parameter
    tables, and the positive chain plus the tampering negatives pass through the
    real verifier.
    
    partial progress

